{#
  The slip, as hidden fields, so every form on the scan console carries the whole of it forward.

  The console's state has always lived in the URL and nowhere else — that is what makes the back
  button undo a mis-scan and the URL something a supervisor can be handed — and it now carries the
  identity captured for each product beside the count, not only the count (item 67).

  Five keys, short because a receiver sees them in the address bar:
    q  units counted with no identity of their own
    s  serials, one per unit
    b  the batch code captured for this product on this slip
    e  the expiry on that batch
    u  the receiver having said these units carry no identity at all

  In ONE partial because there are four forms on that screen and each of them has to carry all of
  it. The screen used to repeat the `q` loop three times, which is three places to forget a key the
  day a sixth one is added.
#}
{% for line in lines %}
    {% if line.quantity > 0 %}
        <input type="hidden" name="q[{{ line.product.id }}]" value="{{ line.quantity }}">
    {% endif %}
    {% for serial in line.serials %}
        <input type="hidden" name="s[{{ line.product.id }}][]" value="{{ serial }}">
    {% endfor %}
    {% if line.lot %}
        <input type="hidden" name="b[{{ line.product.id }}]" value="{{ line.lot }}">
    {% endif %}
    {% if line.expiry %}
        <input type="hidden" name="e[{{ line.product.id }}]" value="{{ line.expiry }}">
    {% endif %}
    {% if line.unidentified %}
        <input type="hidden" name="u[{{ line.product.id }}]" value="1">
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
